    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Description\n\nI would like to be able to map separate bindings for jumping forwards and backwards within the lua setup function (I.E. s for jump forwards, S for jump backwards). I was able to accomplish this via vimscript, but it would be nice to be able to have all of my mini mappings contained within my mini.nvim setup file.",
